# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/bin/
**/obj/
[Bb]uild-out/
extension/dist/
extension/out/
# VS Code test-runner downloads; the extension-host suite creates these at the repo root too
**/.vscode-test/
.npm-cache-do-not-use/
.dotnet-temp/
.dotnet-home/
.nuget-local/
# CLI --set-tsitems / --set-* edit-preview output (regenerable; never committed)
*.edited.txt
# CLI --save dry-run splice preview (engine/Program.cs writes "<file>.spliced.txt"); regenerable, never committed
*.spliced.txt
# engines published into the extension for packaging (generated by `npm run bundle-engine[-net48]`)
extension/engine/
extension/engine-net48/
# LICENSE / CHANGELOG / THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES copied into the extension at package time (copy-license / copy-changelog / copy-notices)
extension/LICENSE
extension/CHANGELOG.md
extension/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
*.vsix

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .NET / Visual Studio (note: extension/.vscode/ is intentionally tracked —
# launch.json drives the F5 dev loop, see CONTRIBUTING.md)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
*.user
*.suo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs, crash dumps, scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.stackdump
*.tmp
extension/tmp/
.agent-scratch/
.codex-tmp/

# Engine / e2e render artifacts (regenerated on every run)
/extender-render.png
/menustrip-render.png
/tooltip-render.png
extension/e2e-render.png
engine/bin/**/*.png
# net48 engine spike render-proof screenshots (not part of the build)
engine-net48/*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal planning notes & local AI tooling (not part of the public repo)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
docs/plans/
docs/handoffs/
docs/maps/
# Local per-release completion records (1.4.0 predates this rule and stays tracked).
docs/release-*-completion-plan.md
run-codex.cmd
test_handler_regex.js

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Visual Studio reference traces: scenario-level retention
#
# scripts/capture-visual-studio-reference-traces.ps1 writes one directory per capture
# RUN, and a run holds every scenario it happened to sweep — 69 runs, 3948 files, 51 MB.
# Only the 40 scenario directories that docs/v2/vs-parity-scenario-catalog.tsv actually
# cites are release evidence (284 files, 5.8 MB); scripts/validate-v2-scenario-catalog.ps1
# verifies exactly those manifests and screenshot hashes. The rest is raw capture history:
# 32 fully superseded runs, plus the scenario folders no PASS row references inside the 37
# runs kept below. It stays on disk for the author and out of the repository.
#
# Regenerate this block from the catalog rather than editing it by hand: a run/scenario
# pair only belongs here while a row with referenceTraceStatus=PASS names it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/v2/reference-traces/*
!docs/v2/reference-traces/README.md
!docs/v2/reference-traces/VS18.0-20260821T082946Z/
docs/v2/reference-traces/VS18.0-20260821T082946Z/*
